course: dictionary
lesson: 12600
title: When colour goes wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Discoloration means a change in the usual colour of something, often to a worse colour. Look at the clues around it: «The white wall had a yellow discoloration near the window, where the sun had shone for years.» The wall was white, and now there is a yellow patch, so the colour has changed.
explain: Ask yourself: what has changed colour, and is the change a problem? Try your meaning in the sentence. «The white wall had a yellow change of colour near the window» still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: Discoloration is often a sign that something is wrong. «The apple had a brown discoloration on one side.» The brown patch may mean the apple is going off. Doctors and dentists also look for discoloration to find problems, such as a bruise on your skin.
fact: Discoloration means a change in the usual colour of something, often to a worse colour.
fact: A discoloration can also be a spot or patch where the colour has changed, like a stain or a bruise.
fact: «Discoloration» is usually uncountable (the wall had discoloration), but you can also say «a discoloration» or «discolorations» when you mean spots or patches.
fact: Discoloration can be caused by rust, mould, sun damage, or a stain.
fact: «Discoloration of the teeth» means the teeth have turned a worse colour, such as yellow or brown.
exercise: «The metal gate had a rusty discoloration on its bars.» What does discoloration mean here? | A brand new, shiny coat of paint | A wooden fence post | *A patch where the colour has changed | A loud squeak made by the gate
exercise: Which sentence shows discoloration? | «She ran to the shop for milk.» | «The park was full of children playing.» | «The bike had a shiny new bell.» | *«Her bruised arm had turned purple and blue.»
exercise: «The old cupboard had a dark discoloration near the sink.» What might have caused this? | A new coat of shiny paint | A cupboard door left open | *Water leaking onto the wood | Someone singing nearby
test: Which word is closest in meaning to discoloration? | A loud noise | A set of tools | A shiny finish | *A stain or patch where the colour has changed
test: «The banana had a brown discoloration.» What might this suggest? | The banana has been painted | The banana is brand new | The banana has been cut in half | *The banana is going bad
exam: «Her tooth had a yellow discoloration, so the dentist checked it.» What does discoloration mean? | A gap where a tooth is missing | A new white filling | *A patch where the colour has changed | A sharp pain in the gum
